# AI Trainer Job Copilot

Local tool: collects AI-trainer jobs, analyzes them via OpenAI/Anthropic API keys or logged-in Claude/ChatGPT
(Chrome extension + localhost bridge), and produces tailored resumes and LinkedIn advice. Do NOT use the Cursor
model for job analysis or resume writing; run the `jt` pipelines instead.

## Layout
- `jt/` Python package. CLI entry: `.venv\Scripts\jt` (Windows). Key modules: `llm/` (api + bridge + client),
  `sources/` (ats.py; linkedin.py is profile-text only), `analysis/` (taxonomy, ats, fit),
  `pipelines/` (analyze, tailor, profile, samples),
  `render/resume.py`.
- `prompts/*.md` Jinja prompt templates, one per task; `prompts/_rules.md` holds the no-fabrication rules.
- `config/` models.yaml (task -> provider: auto|openai|anthropic|claude|gpt|manual), sources.yaml, taxonomy.yaml,
  archetypes.yaml.
- `extension/` Chrome MV3 extension (browser path only). All site selectors are in `extension/selectors.json`.
- `profile/people/<slug>.yaml` named candidate profiles (gitignored); active slug in `data/llm_prefs.yaml`.
  `data/jobs.db`, `output/` are gitignored.
- `dashboard/app.py` Streamlit UI (`jt dashboard`) — Overview has the AI engine picker.

## Commands
`jt init`, `jt llm status|engine|test`, `jt ext-config`, `jt bridge serve|status|test`, `jt sources discover`,
`jt collect`, `jt jobs list|show|gaps|status`, `jt analyze <id>|--all-new`, `jt rank`,
`jt questions <id>`, `jt tailor <id>`, `jt profile list|use|import|show|optimize`, `jt samples list|generate|compare`,
`jt octo check|profile-text` (own profile text only — no LinkedIn job scrape), `jt dashboard`. Prefer API keys
(`OPENAI_API_KEY`) for batch analyze; use bridge when the user chooses Claude/ChatGPT browser.

## Rules
- Never fabricate credentials, employers, dates, metrics or tools in resumes, profiles or prompts. Missing facts
  become questions or suggested actions. Samples are always labelled illustrative.
- When claude.ai or chatgpt.com markup changes, edit `extension/selectors.json` only; verify with
  `jt bridge test` and `pytest tests/test_content_script.py`.
- Never collect jobs from LinkedIn. Octo may only fetch the user's own profile text for import.
- Run `.venv\Scripts\python -m pytest tests -q` after changes (offline; uses fakes, no accounts touched).
- Windows + PowerShell: chain commands with `;`, and use the venv Python explicitly.
